#! /usr/local/share/hexwalk/venv/bin/python
# ===================================================
#
# NAME
#     hexwalk - keyword-based binary and firmware analysis tool
#
# SYNOPSIS
#     hexwalk [OPTIONS] <file>
#
# DESCRIPTION
#     HexWalk is a terminal-based analysis tool for inspecting raw binaries
#     and Intel HEX files using categorized keyword lists and pattern rules.
#     It scans files for embedded strings, configuration artifacts, credentials,
#     and other indicators commonly found in firmware, executables, and system
#     binaries.
#
#     Results are presented in an interactive curses-based interface with
#     category navigation, hit inspection, and a byte-accurate hex viewer.
#
# FEATURES
#     - Supports raw binaries and Intel HEX files
#     - Category-based keyword scanning
#     - Regex-based pattern matching
#     - Interactive TUI with hex and ASCII views
#     - Per-hit modal inspection with navigation
#     - Summary and export capabilities
#
# OPTIONS
#     -h, --help
#         Show help text and exit.
#
#     --version
#         Show version information and exit.
#
# INPUT
#     <file>
#         File to analyze. Can be a raw binary or Intel HEX file.
#
# FILES
#     /usr/local/share/hexwalk/*.txt
#         Keyword and rule definition files, one category per file.
#
# OUTPUT
#     hexwalk_<filename>_export.json
#         JSON export of all findings.
#
#     hexwalk_<filename>_summary.txt
#         Human-readable summary of findings.
#
# EXIT STATUS
#     0   Successful execution
#     1   Invalid arguments or file error
#
# AUTHOR
#     curiousmaster
#
# URL
#     https://github.com/curiousmaster/hexwalk
#
# LICENSE
#     MIT License
#
# ===================================================
